From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: round compressed active width up for DSI

Uke's O82 interface has 1600 active pixels, 10 bits per component and an
8-bpp compressed stream. Truncation gives 426 active pixel clocks while
the DSI host rounds up to 427. With the same pixel clock and porches, the
two timing engines then disagree on every line's period.

Match the DSI host and the exact Uke OEM timing conversion, which uses
drm_fixp2int_ceil() after dividing active width by the compression ratio.
The source comparison is Xiaomi display-drivers,
revision 44275c404a677d9d9e5230fedd1af2ef02fc7b9a,
msm/sde/sde_encoder_phys_vid.c, drm_mode_to_intf_timing_params().

This patch is staged only for the isolated native display profile. It
does not qualify panel output or change the supported firmware scanout.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -134,8 +134,8 @@ static void drm_mode_to_intf_timing_params(
 		 * TODO: replace drm_dsc_get_bpp_int with logic to handle
 		 * fractional part if there is fraction
 		 */
-		timing->width = timing->width * drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc) /
-				(dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
+		timing->width = DIV_ROUND_UP(timing->width * drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc),
+					     dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
 		timing->xres = timing->width;
 		timing->dce_bytes_per_line = msm_dsc_get_bytes_per_line(dsc);
 	}
